cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research software or its evidence, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Structural versus surface historical analogy in geopolitical oil events"
authors:
  - family-names: Delany
    given-names: Joseph
    email: joseph.delany21@gmail.com
    affiliation: "Colby College"
version: "3.0"
date-released: "2026-09-03"
repository-code: "https://github.com/josephdelany/ripple-engine"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - historical analogy
  - geopolitical risk
  - oil markets
  - walk-forward evaluation
  - proper scoring rules
abstract: >-
  A registered walk-forward experiment compares structural state similarity with
  event-class matching on identical prior-event support. Across 264 forecast dates,
  structural weighting improves mean CRPS relative to surface matching, but is not
  distinguishable from uniform historical pooling at the registered 20-trading-day
  horizon. The evidence shows that surface-label filtering can discard useful
  precedents; it does not establish production forecasting skill.
references:
